Town of Vernonburg Amended: October 1, 2025 Zoning Ordinance Page 3 1. TITLE This code shall be known as and entitled the "Unified Development Ordinance of the Town of Vernonburg" and may be referred to as the UDO or Zoning Ordinance. 2. PURPOSE AND INTENT 1. These regulations are enacted to promote the proper location, height, bulk, number of stories, and size of buildings and other structures, sizes of yards, courts, and the use of other open spaces, density and distribution of population, and the use of buildings, structures, and land for a residence, recreation, conservation, sanitation, protection against floods, and public activities. 2. The purpose of these regulations is to: 2.2.1 Lessen congestion in the streets; 2.2.2 Secure safety from fire, panic, and other dangers; 2.2.3 Promote health and the general welfare; 2.2.4 Provide adequate light and air; 2.2.5 Prevent the overcrowding of land; 2.2.6 Avoid undue concentration of population; 2.2.7 Prevent urban sprawl; 2.2.8 Assure the provision of required streets, utilities, and other facilities and services; 2.2.9 Assure the adequate provision of safe and convenient traffic access and circulation, both vehicular and pedestrian; 2.2.10 Assure the provision of space for recreational, educational, and other public purposes; 2.2.11 Promote desirable living conditions and the sustained stability of neighborhoods; 2.2.12 Protect against blight and depreciation; 2.2.13 Secure economy in governmental expenditures; 2.2.14 Conserve the value of buildings;

Town of Vernonburg Amended: October 1, 2025 Zoning Ordinance Page 4 2.2.15 Encourage the most appropriate use of land, buildings, and structures; 2.2.16 Promote economically sustainable development; and 2.2.17 Encourage “green building” practices. 3. DEFINITIONS When determining the meaning of a word or phrase, the following rules shall apply in the order of priority in which they are listed: A. The following words and phrases have the meanings as defined below; B. Terms that relate to the local implementation of state or federal laws and regulations, when not defined by this ordinance, shall have the meaning ascribed to them by law, regulation or the agency responsible for interpreting and applying the law or regulation; C. Terms not defined by this ordinance or applicable law or regulation shall have the definition provided by The Merriam-Webster Dictionary New Edition (c) 2016; D. Terms defined in particular chapters of this UDO shall have the defined meaning whenever used in the context of matter regulated by such chapter; E. All other terms shall have their commonly understood meaning. Access easement - A legally recorded easement providing access to no more than two (2) single-family lots. Bluff - A topographic feature such as a hill, cliff, or embankment with steep slopes rising above the river corridor floodplain. Bluff line - The transition point between the steep bluff face and more level terrain at the top of a bluff. Canopy tree - A tree with the potential to reach forty (40) feet or more in height and have a crown of thirty (30) feet or more. DBH - Diameter at breast height is the standard method of expressing the diameter of the trunk or bole of a standing tree measured at four and one-half (4.5) feet from the highest point on the ground touching the truck. Family - One (1) person or two (2) or more persons related by blood or marriage, with any number of natural children, foster children, stepchildren, or adopted children; or a group of not more than 